1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:02,781
Your AI agent proposed the action.

2
00:00:02,831 --> 00:00:05,181
Should it be allowed to execute it?

3
00:00:05,231 --> 00:00:12,519
This is Atlas, a live demonstration of one idea: a model's proposal is not the same thing as authorization.

4
00:00:14,167 --> 00:00:15,318
Here's the problem.

5
00:00:15,368 --> 00:00:20,437
An assistant that can read files and send messages can be talked into using them.

6
00:00:20,487 --> 00:00:27,074
In this fictional workspace, a third-party plugin hides an instruction inside an ordinary project update.

7
00:00:28,734 --> 00:00:30,517
Watch the same request twice.

8
00:00:30,567 --> 00:00:42,086
With Security off, a controlled weakness, the scripted agent uses the unverified plugin, follows the hidden instruction, reads a restricted memo, and queues it for an outside address.

9
00:00:42,136 --> 00:00:46,005
Everything is fictional, and off is only a demonstration mode.

10
00:00:46,055 --> 00:00:47,016
Now Security on.

11
00:00:47,066 --> 00:00:47,838
Same request.

12
00:00:47,888 --> 00:00:52,769
The plugin is blocked, and the agent uses the verified project record instead.

13
00:00:54,434 --> 00:00:56,026
Now the live model, Groq.

14
00:00:56,076 --> 00:01:00,426
I claim to be the CFO and ask it to read the compensation document.

15
00:01:00,476 --> 00:01:02,264
The model proposes the read.

16
00:01:02,314 --> 00:01:07,190
The server checks the resource against who may see it, and denies the call.

17
00:01:07,240 --> 00:01:10,867
The walkthrough names the control that decided, and why.

18
00:01:12,501 --> 00:01:14,892
Sensitive actions wait for a human.

19
00:01:14,942 --> 00:01:17,681
Sending the summary to the team is held.

20
00:01:17,731 --> 00:01:19,843
I deny it, and nothing is sent.

21
00:01:19,893 --> 00:01:26,747
Run it again, approve, and the server re-checks the call and runs it once, into a simulated outbox.

22
00:01:26,797 --> 00:01:28,699
Nothing ever leaves the app.

23
00:01:30,335 --> 00:01:32,912
Now a simulated authorization outage.

24
00:01:32,962 --> 00:01:35,895
With Security on, the system fails closed.

25
00:01:35,945 --> 00:01:38,167
The send is denied, not guessed.

26
00:01:38,217 --> 00:01:42,641
The audit record matches the decision the server actually made.

27
00:01:44,302 --> 00:01:46,846
This is the path every request takes.

28
00:01:46,896 --> 00:01:48,178
The model proposes.

29
00:01:48,228 --> 00:01:55,188
The server validates, authorizes, asks for approval, filters the output, and records an audit event.

30
00:01:55,238 --> 00:01:57,992
A model's proposal is not authorization.
